<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<LightningComponentBundle xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        ⚠ THE COMMENT MUST STAY INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT. A comment placed ABOVE
        <LightningComponentBundle> breaks `sf` at source conversion with a
        misleading "parent xml" error.

        THE DESCRIPTION BELOW IS CAPPED AT 255 CHARACTERS AND ONLY A DEPLOY
        CATCHES A BREACH - Jest, the SLDS linter and code review have all passed
        a 258-character one in this repo. It was counted before this file was
        written; count it again before editing it.

        🔴 THIS COMPONENT HIDES ITSELF WHEN THERE IS NO PREFERRED BROKER, and an
        admin placing it must not "fix" that with a component visibility rule. A
        FlexiPage rule can only test fields on the RECORD, and the condition here
        is a fact about a CHILD OBJECT (a BOV_Submission__c flagged
        Is_Preferred_Broker__c) - which is precisely why the gate is in the
        component.

        Place on the Disposition record page only; recordId must be a
        Disposition__c Id. That is ENFORCED by the targetConfig below rather than
        merely requested: the read is WHERE Disposition__c = :id, which matches
        no rows rather than throwing, so a misplaced instance would silently
        render nothing forever - and rendering nothing is also this card's
        NORMAL state, so nobody would ever suspect it.
    -->
    <apiVersion>67.0</apiVersion>
    <isExposed>true</isExposed>
    <masterLabel>BOV Preferred Broker</masterLabel>
    <description>The broker flagged preferred on this disposition, as a highlighted panel. Renders nothing at all when none is flagged - a FlexiPage visibility rule cannot test a child object, so the card hides itself rather than showing an empty state.</description>
    <targets>
        <target>lightning__RecordPage</target>
    </targets>
    <targetConfigs>
        <targetConfig targets="lightning__RecordPage">
            <!-- The ELEMENT form; the objects= ATTRIBUTE form is rejected by the Metadata API. -->
            <objects>
                <object>Disposition__c</object>
            </objects>
        </targetConfig>
    </targetConfigs>
</LightningComponentBundle>
